WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:34.400
<b>Calm Belt</b>

3
00:02:43.460 --> 00:02:46.270
Damn! That is the biggest
Sea King I've ever seen!

4
00:02:46.270 --> 00:02:48.370
Why is it flipping out? It's scary!

5
00:02:48.370 --> 00:02:50.970
[SEA KING roars]

6
00:02:57.080 --> 00:02:59.480
[PENGUIN]
It's dead! Something killed it!

7
00:02:59.480 --> 00:03:01.920
[SHACHI whimpers]
You gotta be joking!

8
00:02:59.830 --> 00:03:05.460
<b>Cheer</b>

9
00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:03.760
[PENGUIN]
I didn't get a look at what happened.

10
00:03:03.760 --> 00:03:05.930
[BEPO]
I don't think I like this place!

11
00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:10.730
[HEART PIRATES gasp]

12
00:03:10.730 --> 00:03:11.700
[PENGUIN]
Is that a man?

13
00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:13.700
[SHACHI]
Hey! Who're you?

14
00:03:13.700 --> 00:03:16.540
[PENGUIN, SHACHI gasping]

15
00:03:16.540 --> 00:03:18.170
[RAYLEIGH sighs]
What a doozy.

16
00:03:18.170 --> 00:03:19.010
[HEART PIRATES gasp]

17
00:03:19.010 --> 00:03:20.510
- It's you.
- [RAYLEIGH sighs]

18
00:03:21.890 --> 00:03:25.360
You're the... The Dark
King Silvers Rayleigh!

19
00:03:25.360 --> 00:03:26.560
[HEART PIRATES]
What?

20
00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:28.290
Oh, it's been a while.

21
00:03:28.290 --> 00:03:30.760
I remember meeting you at Sabaody.

22
00:03:35.380 --> 00:03:38.410
It's Gold Roger's first mate,
right here in the flesh.

23
00:03:38.410 --> 00:03:40.050
[RAYLEIGH]
So, funny story.

24
00:03:40.050 --> 00:03:42.120
Things got kind of rocky in the storm.

25
00:03:42.120 --> 00:03:44.720
My ship sank so I had
no choice but to swim here.

26
00:03:44.720 --> 00:03:45.860
What?!

27
00:03:45.860 --> 00:03:47.880
But they never have storms
in this part of the sea,

28
00:03:47.880 --> 00:03:49.920
that's why they call it the Calm Belt!

29
00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:51.080
But then that must mean...

30
00:03:51.080 --> 00:03:54.650
He crashed in safe waters and swam
through that bed of Sea Kings?

31
00:03:54.650 --> 00:03:57.090
How is that supposed to work?

32
00:03:57.090 --> 00:03:58.890
[RAYLEIGH]
I have a pretty good breaststroke.

33
00:03:58.890 --> 00:04:01.120
[PENGUIN]
Right. He says
it like it's no big deal.

34
00:04:01.120 --> 00:04:04.150
[SHACHI]
So, you killed that giant thing...

35
00:04:04.150 --> 00:04:05.650
[SHACHI, PENGUIN]
– ...with your bare hands?
– ...with your bare hands?

36
00:04:05.650 --> 00:04:09.380
[BEPO]
I have actual bear hands
and I couldn't do that!

37
00:04:09.380 --> 00:04:10.980
[yelps]

38
00:04:10.980 --> 00:04:12.550
Forgive me, Dark King.

39
00:04:12.550 --> 00:04:14.080
[SHACHI, PENGUIN]
– What are you even sorry for?
– What are you even sorry for?

40
00:04:14.080 --> 00:04:15.220
[BEPO]
Sorry!

41
00:04:15.220 --> 00:04:17.020
Let me be frank.

42
00:04:17.020 --> 00:04:18.920
[LAW grunts]

43
00:04:18.920 --> 00:04:22.320
Something tells me Luffy's on
this island. Is that correct?

44
00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:23.750
[LAW gasps]

45
00:04:26.920 --> 00:04:28.160
[MARGARET]
Have you heard the news?

46
00:04:28.160 --> 00:04:33.130
The princess and some others just left
to deliver food to Luffy! They're so lucky!

47
00:04:28.180 --> 00:04:32.820
<b>Center of the Island
 Isle of Women, Amazon Lily</b>

48
00:04:33.130 --> 00:04:35.800
I wanna make those cheeks of his stretch
and stretch and stretch and stretch...

49
00:04:35.800 --> 00:04:37.130
[MARGARET]
I heard they'll invite him over

50
00:04:37.130 --> 00:04:39.340
once all his wounds heal.
It should be any day now!

51
00:04:39.340 --> 00:04:41.770
[SWEET PEA]
We should hold a feast again!

52
00:04:41.770 --> 00:04:45.010
[APHELANDRA]
A shame he's hurt, but I'm
glad he came back so soon!

53
00:04:45.890 --> 00:04:48.160
Well, since he's here again,
maybe I'll make him another

54
00:04:48.160 --> 00:04:50.360
pair of clothes,
without all the frills!

55
00:04:50.360 --> 00:04:53.570
[ALL laughing]

56
00:04:55.640 --> 00:04:57.640
[HANCOCK]
How shameful it is for newlyweds

57
00:04:57.640 --> 00:05:01.140
to be separated like this! What
a tragic heroine I've become!

58
00:05:01.140 --> 00:05:02.010
[NYON grunts]

59
00:05:02.010 --> 00:05:04.080
"Sweetie, don't say that."

60
00:05:04.080 --> 00:05:06.500
"You know, we're always
together in spirit!"

61
00:05:06.500 --> 00:05:07.660
"Of course, dear!"

62
00:05:07.660 --> 00:05:09.930
"No matter how far apart
the world may keep us,

63
00:05:09.930 --> 00:05:12.140
we are bound by a thread of passion!"

64
00:05:12.140 --> 00:05:14.160
"Oh, Luffy!"

65
00:05:14.160 --> 00:05:16.140
You always know just what to say!

66
00:05:16.140 --> 00:05:18.110
My heart is aflame with affection!

67
00:05:18.110 --> 00:05:20.600
I can feel the desire
building up inside me!

68
00:05:20.600 --> 00:05:23.070
You are hopeless! How foolish!

69
00:05:23.070 --> 00:05:25.830
I've told you. Any man
may remember your name,

70
00:05:25.830 --> 00:05:28.830
but that doesn't mean
that you're married!

71
00:05:28.830 --> 00:05:31.040
Oh? Then what is marriage?

72
00:05:31.040 --> 00:05:32.040
What else is there to do?

73
00:05:32.040 --> 00:05:35.310
That is a difficult question to answer.

74
00:05:37.940 --> 00:05:41.570
[JIMBEI]
You're too weak to travel to Sabaody,
especially with that wound.

75
00:05:41.570 --> 00:05:42.840
[LUFFY]
I'll make it work.

76
00:05:42.840 --> 00:05:45.340
I gotta see my friends
as soon as possible.

77
00:05:45.340 --> 00:05:46.780
They'll be expecting me.

78
00:05:46.780 --> 00:05:48.590
I promised them I'd be there.

79
00:05:48.590 --> 00:05:50.520
Well, nevertheless...

80
00:05:52.020 --> 00:05:54.420
[JIMBEI]
Now, that's odd. The submarine is gone.

81
00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:56.730
Surely they didn't depart?

82
00:05:56.730 --> 00:05:58.500
Oh, hello there, Luffy!

83
00:05:58.500 --> 00:06:01.130
Wha...? It's Rayleigh, the old guy!

84
00:06:01.130 --> 00:06:04.140
[chuckles]
Straightforward
as ever, I see.

85
00:06:04.140 --> 00:06:05.680
[LUFFY]
But why are you here?

86
00:06:05.680 --> 00:06:08.720
I was about to use my
Vivre Card to go to Sabaody

87
00:06:08.720 --> 00:06:10.880
since my friends
should be waiting there.

88
00:06:12.480 --> 00:06:13.780
So, did you see them?

89
00:06:13.780 --> 00:06:17.250
I haven't. Actually, it seems
they haven't made it there yet.

90
00:06:17.250 --> 00:06:21.390
As for my Vivre Card, I ended up
handing it off to Shakky.

91
00:06:21.390 --> 00:06:23.020
It's rather nice.

92
00:06:23.020 --> 00:06:26.820
No one can find me and
I can go wherever I please!

93
00:06:26.820 --> 00:06:30.030
Dark King Rayleigh!
I don't believe this.

94
00:06:30.030 --> 00:06:31.260
Is it really you?

95
00:06:31.260 --> 00:06:34.120
[RAYLEIGH]
Hm. You must be that former Warlord.

96
00:06:35.120 --> 00:06:36.120
Something wrong?

97
00:06:36.120 --> 00:06:40.450
I didn't expect to come
face-to-face with a living legend.

98
00:06:40.450 --> 00:06:43.320
[RAYLEIGH]
Ah, I suppose you'd like your hat back.

99
00:06:43.320 --> 00:06:44.860
[LUFFY]
Oh, yeah. Thanks!

100
00:06:45.860 --> 00:06:47.690
[LUFFY chuckles]

101
00:06:49.400 --> 00:06:51.780
My head just doesn't
feel right without it!

102
00:06:51.780 --> 00:06:54.200
There, that's a lot better!

103
00:06:54.200 --> 00:06:55.500
[JIMBEI grunts]

104
00:06:56.600 --> 00:06:59.910
[JIMBEI]
Have you seen a group of pirates
or a submarine around here?

105
00:06:59.910 --> 00:07:03.920
[RAYLEIGH]
If you're talking about
Trafalgar Law, he took off.

106
00:07:03.920 --> 00:07:06.060
He left a message for Luffy.

107
00:07:06.060 --> 00:07:08.390
"Stay in bed for two more weeks."

108
00:07:10.690 --> 00:07:12.800
[RAYLEIGH]
He saved your life, didn't he?

109
00:07:18.320 --> 00:07:21.720
Now that was a raw deal.
All those women right there.

110
00:07:21.720 --> 00:07:25.030
And we were stuck on
the shore. Man, what a tease.

111
00:07:25.030 --> 00:07:26.950
They said bears were
welcome to visit, though.

112
00:07:26.950 --> 00:07:28.620
[SHACHI, PENGUIN]
– Hey, don't tell us that!
– Hey, don't tell us that!

113
00:07:28.620 --> 00:07:29.580
[BEPO]
I'm sorry.

114
00:07:29.580 --> 00:07:31.590
[SHACHI, PENGUIN]
– Who cares?!
– Who cares?!

115
00:07:31.590 --> 00:07:34.230
I wonder what the Dark King is up to.

116
00:07:34.230 --> 00:07:37.180
Seems he's drawn to another
man with the Will of D.

117
00:07:37.180 --> 00:07:41.630
Heh. Well, whatever happens,
it's bound to be a storm.

118
00:07:41.630 --> 00:07:46.110
[NYON]
Nyo! It can't be!
Rayleigh, is that really you?

119
00:07:46.110 --> 00:07:48.650
[RAYLEIGH]
Oh, why hello, Gloriosa!

120
00:07:48.650 --> 00:07:50.280
It sure has been awhile!

121
00:07:50.280 --> 00:07:51.480
Hi, Rayleigh!

122
00:07:51.480 --> 00:07:52.690
How're you?

123
00:07:52.690 --> 00:07:55.020
[RAYLEIGH]
I'm lovely! Good to see you!

124
00:07:55.020 --> 00:07:56.350
It's Luffy!

125
00:07:56.350 --> 00:07:58.290
[SANDERSONIA, MARIGOLD]
– Could you show some manners for once?
– Could you show some manners for once?

126
00:07:58.290 --> 00:07:59.730
Don't ignore the man
who saved your life!

127
00:07:59.730 --> 00:08:00.480
He "saved your life"?

128
00:08:02.010 --> 00:08:04.380
So, the three of you know
old man Rayleigh, too?

129
00:08:04.380 --> 00:08:05.650
Indeed!

130
00:08:05.650 --> 00:08:08.340
It's a long story.
We'll spare you the details.

131
00:08:08.340 --> 00:08:10.250
[HANCOCK]
I'm so glad to see that you're well.

132
00:08:10.250 --> 00:08:12.890
I've been awake for days,
worrying about you.

133
00:08:12.890 --> 00:08:15.360
You must be starving!
I've brought plenty of food.

134
00:08:15.360 --> 00:08:18.110
Please, eat to your heart's content.

135
00:08:18.110 --> 00:08:20.050
[NYON]
You can't even bear to look at him.

136
00:08:20.050 --> 00:08:22.760
How is this "marriage" of
yours supposed to work out?

137
00:08:22.760 --> 00:08:25.060
[HANCOCK]
Serve the man!

138
00:08:25.060 --> 00:08:27.400
Give him some food,
and be quick about it!

139
00:08:27.400 --> 00:08:29.950
[stomach rumbling]

140
00:08:29.950 --> 00:08:30.680
[JIMBEI grunts]

141
00:08:30.680 --> 00:08:32.220
No, Jimbei!

142
00:08:32.220 --> 00:08:34.950
This cornucopia was not meant for you!

143
00:08:34.950 --> 00:08:36.920
You may have one bite.

144
00:08:36.920 --> 00:08:38.720
[JIMBEI]
How generous.

145
00:08:38.720 --> 00:08:41.560
I shall endeavor to curb my appetite.

146
00:08:43.090 --> 00:08:45.630
Come, Luffy. You need your strength.

147
00:08:45.630 --> 00:08:48.900
And as they say, "to eat is to live."

148
00:08:51.500 --> 00:08:54.270
[stomach rumbling]

149
00:09:04.010 --> 00:09:07.220
Well done! Back to
the old Luffy already!

150
00:09:09.190 --> 00:09:11.820
[NYON]
Hm? A letter from Shakky!

151
00:09:11.820 --> 00:09:14.260
Thank you for bringing this, Rayleigh.

152
00:09:14.260 --> 00:09:17.930
She hasn't changed, nyot one bit.

153
00:09:17.930 --> 00:09:20.700
Yeah. If you were
living in Sabaody again,

154
00:09:20.700 --> 00:09:24.000
it'd be just like old times.
She's doing well.

155
00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:28.010
And you girls, you three have
gotten tough over the past 13 years,

156
00:09:28.010 --> 00:09:31.080
possessing a strength that is
only matched by your beauty.

157
00:09:31.080 --> 00:09:34.250
Rayleigh, Granny Nyon, and Shakky.

158
00:09:34.250 --> 00:09:35.520
If it weren't for you three,

159
00:09:35.520 --> 00:09:39.690
we'd still be slaves to the
Celestial Dragons right now.

160
00:09:39.690 --> 00:09:43.000
This troubles me. If you found him,

161
00:09:43.000 --> 00:09:46.910
protecting Luffy may be more
difficult than we thought.

162
00:09:46.910 --> 00:09:50.680
I knyow you're friends, but if
you could find Luffy so quickly,

163
00:09:50.680 --> 00:09:54.570
I fear the Navy's search for him
may prove successful as well.

164
00:09:54.570 --> 00:09:56.300
Then we'd all be in danger.

165
00:09:56.300 --> 00:10:00.370
Ah. If it isn't Rayleigh!
It's me, Hancock!

166
00:10:00.370 --> 00:10:01.970
Do you remember me?

167
00:10:01.970 --> 00:10:04.850
Really? You just now nyoticed him?!

168
00:10:04.850 --> 00:10:06.080
[chuckles]

169
00:10:06.080 --> 00:10:09.820
Don't worry, I doubt the Navy will
guess that Luffy's staying here.

170
00:10:10.820 --> 00:10:14.750
[RAYLEIGH]
First off, the one who helped him
escape from the Sabaody Archipelago

171
00:10:14.750 --> 00:10:17.260
told me he sent him off
in this direction.

172
00:10:19.150 --> 00:10:21.490
[KUMA]
I work for the Revolutionary Army.

173
00:10:21.490 --> 00:10:25.490
Because Straw Hat shares a connection
with Dragon, I will let his crew escape.

174
00:10:25.490 --> 00:10:26.560
[RAYLEIGH]
Hm?

175
00:10:26.560 --> 00:10:30.000
[SHAKKY]
Oh? That's quite the twist.

176
00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:33.820
So, where did he end up
sending our Monkey boy?

177
00:10:33.820 --> 00:10:35.220
Beats me.

178
00:10:38.310 --> 00:10:42.080
[KUMA]
I apologize for
my abrupt manner earlier.

179
00:10:42.080 --> 00:10:44.320
Can I speak with you for a moment?

180
00:10:45.330 --> 00:10:49.270
I don't have much time, not as myself.

181
00:10:49.270 --> 00:10:51.040
[RAYLEIGH]
Hm?

182
00:10:51.040 --> 00:10:53.670
Now, as for Straw Hat...

183
00:10:53.670 --> 00:10:58.110
Kuma would only tell me what direction
he sent our friend Luffy flying in.

184
00:10:58.110 --> 00:11:01.160
But even that info didn't
necessarily point to this island.

185
00:11:01.160 --> 00:11:03.060
I spent a lot of time puzzling over

186
00:11:03.060 --> 00:11:07.230
how Luffy was able to infiltrate
such a heavily guarded prison.

187
00:11:07.230 --> 00:11:09.770
It made enough sense that Luffy
got there by stowing away

188
00:11:09.770 --> 00:11:13.670
on a Navy ship with Hancock,
but it still didn't add up.

189
00:11:13.670 --> 00:11:17.410
[NYON]
Hmm.

190
00:11:17.410 --> 00:11:20.940
[RAYLEIGH]
Hancock is known to hate both
the World Government and men.

191
00:11:20.940 --> 00:11:25.650
I don't think she'd willingly get on
a government ship, certainly not to help a man.

192
00:11:26.780 --> 00:11:29.950
Knowing that, how else would
Luffy have gotten there?

193
00:11:29.950 --> 00:11:32.150
[SHAKKY]
Have you considered this one?

194
00:11:33.490 --> 00:11:38.390
Maybe Hancock met Monkey and had
a case of "love at first sight."

195
00:11:38.390 --> 00:11:40.700
If so, everything fits.

196
00:11:42.730 --> 00:11:45.200
[SHAKKY]
He is pretty cute, after all.

197
00:11:46.770 --> 00:11:51.390
It's also a lovely way to spite the Navy,
and now she's got the perfect opportunity

198
00:11:51.390 --> 00:11:54.360
to nurse her poor, injured
loverboy back to health.

199
00:11:54.770 --> 00:11:57.170
[laughs]
I think you're
letting your imagination

200
00:11:57.170 --> 00:11:58.850
get carried away, Shakky!

201
00:12:01.180 --> 00:12:04.860
[RAYLEIGH]
Guess that's the
power of women's intuition.

202
00:12:04.860 --> 00:12:06.660
That's my Shakky!

203
00:12:06.660 --> 00:12:10.030
The Snake Princess is,
well, see for yourself.

204
00:12:10.030 --> 00:12:14.000
[HANCOCK]
Do you like it? Please
say yes! It's all just for you!

205
00:12:14.000 --> 00:12:18.740
Although our little theory turned out
to be true, it's still pretty ridiculous,

206
00:12:18.740 --> 00:12:21.400
so the Navy won't act on it.

207
00:12:21.400 --> 00:12:24.400
All right. It's time
we got down to business.

208
00:12:25.410 --> 00:12:27.380
[RAYLEIGH]
Hey, Luffy.

209
00:12:27.380 --> 00:12:29.770
Earlier you said you're
heading back to Sabaody

210
00:12:29.770 --> 00:12:33.080
to meet up with your crew.
Do you still plan on doing that?

211
00:12:35.550 --> 00:12:38.250
Of course, I do. They need me.

212
00:12:39.650 --> 00:12:43.490
Maybe they do, but is
that the best choice?

213
00:12:43.490 --> 00:12:45.190
[LUFFY grunts]

214
00:12:49.500 --> 00:12:53.100
Surely, you remember how your
last trip to Sabaody ended.

215
00:12:53.100 --> 00:12:54.610
[gasps]

216
00:13:00.580 --> 00:13:01.780
Everyone!

217
00:13:01.780 --> 00:13:04.950
Start running and
look after yourselves!

218
00:13:04.950 --> 00:13:09.220
We can't win this one! We're too weak!

219
00:13:09.220 --> 00:13:11.020
Get moving!

220
00:13:13.380 --> 00:13:16.050
I couldn't save any of them.

221
00:13:16.050 --> 00:13:18.520
What's wrong with me?

222
00:13:18.520 --> 00:13:23.490
[LUFFY crying]

223
00:13:30.300 --> 00:13:33.270
As you are right now, do you
think you would fare any better

224
00:13:33.270 --> 00:13:35.970
if you were to face
those enemies again?

225
00:13:52.420 --> 00:13:54.120
I know, but I...

226
00:13:54.120 --> 00:13:59.230
[RAYLEIGH]
Do you want to be reunited with your
friends, only to endure the same fate?

227
00:13:59.230 --> 00:14:00.360
[LUFFY grunts]

228
00:14:00.360 --> 00:14:03.860
I would imagine that your answer is no.

229
00:14:03.860 --> 00:14:06.900
So let me offer you some advice.

230
00:14:06.900 --> 00:14:08.670
Do with it what you will.

231
00:14:16.600 --> 00:14:22.210
<b>Grand Line
Bowin Archipelago</b>

232
00:14:17.380 --> 00:14:21.520
[NARRATOR]
Meanwhile, on the
Bowin Islands on the Grand Line.

233
00:14:23.130 --> 00:14:26.330
[HERACLES]
Come back here, Usopp'n!

234
00:14:26.330 --> 00:14:29.130
[USOPP]
Don't try to stop me!

235
00:14:29.130 --> 00:14:33.270
[NARRATOR]
Usopp seems to
be... moving his massive body,

236
00:14:33.270 --> 00:14:35.430
which has grown huge
from eating an abundant

237
00:14:35.430 --> 00:14:38.170
variety of food from
the Gorging Forest.

238
00:14:40.030 --> 00:14:42.200
[NARRATOR]
Some might call it running.

239
00:14:43.410 --> 00:14:45.180
[HERACLES]
Usopp'n, it's impossible!

240
00:14:45.180 --> 00:14:48.220
[USOPP]
No, it's not!
I'll keep trying till I get it!

241
00:14:48.220 --> 00:14:49.660
I can do it this time!

242
00:14:49.660 --> 00:14:53.060
[GIANT BEETLE bellows]

243
00:14:53.060 --> 00:14:54.590
[panting]

244
00:14:54.590 --> 00:14:56.400
There you are!

245
00:14:56.400 --> 00:14:59.630
[GIANT BEETLE snarls]

246
00:14:59.630 --> 00:15:02.730
[USOPP]
Get out of my way, you big oaf!

247
00:15:02.730 --> 00:15:04.700
Special Attack...

248
00:15:04.700 --> 00:15:07.170
[USOPP groans]

249
00:15:07.170 --> 00:15:10.810
[HERACLES]
Oh, no! Usopp'n!

250
00:15:11.940 --> 00:15:15.610
[USOPP groans]

251
00:15:15.610 --> 00:15:17.950
[HERACLES]
Why won't you heed my warnings?

252
00:15:17.950 --> 00:15:20.180
Damn it. So close.

253
00:15:20.180 --> 00:15:21.690
[HERACLES]
You can't do this!

254
00:15:21.690 --> 00:15:24.550
Every time you try to
get off of the island'n,

255
00:15:24.550 --> 00:15:26.920
terrifying creatures
like the giant beetle'n

256
00:15:26.920 --> 00:15:31.360
will stand in your way and force
you back into the forest'n.

257
00:15:31.360 --> 00:15:34.160
[USOPP grunts]

258
00:15:36.730 --> 00:15:38.030
[HERACLES]
There's nothing to stop you

259
00:15:38.030 --> 00:15:42.240
from entering the island'n,
but then, your fate is sealed!

260
00:15:42.240 --> 00:15:44.740
Even if you can learn
to survive in the forest,

261
00:15:44.740 --> 00:15:47.730
no one ever leaves this island'n alive!

262
00:15:47.730 --> 00:15:52.770
And don't forget,
my name is Heracles'n!

263
00:15:52.770 --> 00:15:55.540
Huh? Usopp'n? Where did you go?

264
00:15:55.540 --> 00:15:57.040
[rumbling]

265
00:15:57.040 --> 00:15:58.110
[HERACLES]
Huh?

266
00:16:01.040 --> 00:16:01.950
[GIANT SEA HIPPO grunts]

267
00:16:01.950 --> 00:16:03.180
[HERACLES]
Oh, no!

268
00:16:03.180 --> 00:16:06.310
The sea creature'n has just
crawled onto the island'n!

269
00:16:06.310 --> 00:16:09.410
Usopp'n! You're in danger!

270
00:16:09.410 --> 00:16:12.680
[HERACLES yells]

271
00:16:12.680 --> 00:16:17.010
[NARRATOR]
The sweet flavors and intoxicating aromas
that emanate from the Bowin Islands

272
00:16:17.010 --> 00:16:20.280
attract a plethora of
giant insects and birds.

273
00:16:20.280 --> 00:16:25.150
Even Sea Kings and other aquatic
animals visit from time to time.

274
00:16:25.150 --> 00:16:26.620
It's a sea hippo!

275
00:16:26.620 --> 00:16:28.690
[GIANT SEA HIPPO snorts, sniffs]

276
00:16:28.690 --> 00:16:31.830
[USOPP]
Now's not the time to stop and stare!

277
00:16:31.830 --> 00:16:34.060
[NARRATOR]
The wonderful smells lead them deeper

278
00:16:34.060 --> 00:16:39.000
onto the island. There, they
find ever more tempting flavors.

279
00:16:42.840 --> 00:16:45.510
[NARRATOR]
But while it's
easy to enter the island...

280
00:16:46.930 --> 00:16:49.700
[NARRATOR]
it's much harder to leave.

281
00:16:49.700 --> 00:16:52.400
[USOPP panting]

282
00:16:52.400 --> 00:16:53.800
- [TEETHED PLANT A growls]
- [USOPP] Another one!

283
00:16:53.800 --> 00:16:56.100
Try my Exploding Star!

284
00:16:58.840 --> 00:17:01.280
I'm getting out of here
no matter what it takes!

285
00:17:01.280 --> 00:17:03.880
Don't you dare get in my way!

286
00:17:08.790 --> 00:17:10.390
[HERACLES]
The islands are gonna move again!

287
00:17:10.390 --> 00:17:12.330
Wait. Do what now?

288
00:17:14.000 --> 00:17:16.200
- [rumbling]
- [USOPP gasps]

289
00:17:16.200 --> 00:17:19.370
[HERACLES]
Usopp'n! Grab a tree and hang on!

290
00:17:19.370 --> 00:17:21.170
[USOPP]
How often does this happen?

291
00:17:21.170 --> 00:17:23.610
[HERACLES]
Every time it needs to feed!

292
00:17:29.480 --> 00:17:33.420
[NARRATOR]
The so-called Bowin Islands are
not at all what they appear.

293
00:17:39.290 --> 00:17:44.290
[screaming]

294
00:17:46.260 --> 00:17:47.800
[NARRATOR]
The flower-shaped island is

295
00:17:47.800 --> 00:17:51.970
actually an island-sized flower
known as the Stomach Baron.

296
00:17:51.970 --> 00:17:53.370
[USOPP screams]

297
00:17:53.370 --> 00:17:56.510
[HERACLES]
Usopp'n!

298
00:17:57.740 --> 00:17:59.620
[USOPP gasps]

299
00:17:59.620 --> 00:18:03.220
[panting]

300
00:18:04.660 --> 00:18:07.060
[HERACLES]
What has gotten into you?

301
00:18:09.010 --> 00:18:12.850
[HERACLES]
Ever since the News Coo brought that paper,
you've been acting like a maniac!

302
00:18:12.850 --> 00:18:13.650
What did it say?

303
00:18:13.650 --> 00:18:17.190
[crying]

304
00:18:17.190 --> 00:18:19.860
[USOPP]
I can't be here!

305
00:18:19.860 --> 00:18:21.930
I have to go!

306
00:18:21.930 --> 00:18:25.000
I've wasted enough time
on this stupid island!

307
00:18:30.400 --> 00:18:34.440
[USOPP]
Luffy, he lost his brother in the war!

308
00:18:35.910 --> 00:18:40.410
And now, he doesn't know where
we are, or if we're alive!

309
00:18:40.410 --> 00:18:45.420
[crying]

310
00:18:58.790 --> 00:19:02.500
Luffy wouldn't let me suffer like that!

311
00:19:02.500 --> 00:19:05.930
I'm his friend! I need
to be there for him!

312
00:19:05.930 --> 00:19:08.740
[USOPP crying]

313
00:19:08.740 --> 00:19:11.350
[USOPP]
I'm sorry, Luffy!

314
00:19:14.330 --> 00:19:18.070
<b>Torino Kingdom</b>

315
00:19:18.500 --> 00:19:20.800
[NATIVE A]
We not long ago make friends.

316
00:19:20.800 --> 00:19:22.570
Raccoon really leave now?

317
00:19:22.570 --> 00:19:24.540
[BIRDS squawk]

318
00:19:24.540 --> 00:19:25.370
[CHOPPER]
Yeah.

319
00:19:25.370 --> 00:19:29.110
As soon as I read that newspaper and found
out what my friend's been going through,

320
00:19:29.110 --> 00:19:33.040
I realized I couldn't
stick around any longer.

321
00:19:33.040 --> 00:19:36.480
[CHOPPER]
I had just met
Luffy's brother in Alabasta.

322
00:19:36.480 --> 00:19:39.570
I can't believe what happened to him!

323
00:19:39.570 --> 00:19:41.840
I'm worried about Luffy.

324
00:19:41.840 --> 00:19:43.840
What if he needs medical attention?

325
00:19:43.840 --> 00:19:46.540
He always pushes himself way too hard.

326
00:19:46.540 --> 00:19:47.890
Good friend.

327
00:19:47.890 --> 00:19:51.700
Anyway, It's good to see you and
the birds are getting along better now.

328
00:19:51.700 --> 00:19:56.570
Understanding only happen because brave
Raccoon friend risking life to do talking!

329
00:19:56.570 --> 00:19:58.730
[CHOPPER]
Aww.

330
00:19:58.730 --> 00:20:01.370
You guys remember not to pick
fights with the humans, okay?

331
00:20:01.370 --> 00:20:03.200
[BIRDS squawk]

332
00:20:03.200 --> 00:20:04.740
[CHOPPER]
They're not gonna hurt you!

333
00:20:04.740 --> 00:20:08.340
They just want you to let them pick
the plants that grow on that tree!

334
00:20:08.340 --> 00:20:10.310
[NATIVE B]
Raccoon speaking truth!

335
00:20:10.310 --> 00:20:14.130
We no fight you or taking eggs.
We not same as bad humans

336
00:20:14.130 --> 00:20:17.870
that stealing your treasure and
chase you away! We your friends!

337
00:20:17.870 --> 00:20:19.240
[BIRDS squawk]

338
00:20:19.240 --> 00:20:21.960
Oh, by the way, I was really
impressed with that medicine

339
00:20:21.960 --> 00:20:24.040
you guys gave me when
I got injured before.

340
00:20:24.040 --> 00:20:25.600
It's great stuff!

341
00:20:25.600 --> 00:20:27.140
See, I'm better already!

342
00:20:27.140 --> 00:20:32.410
Right! We using special medicine recipe
we passing down over many generation!

343
00:20:34.080 --> 00:20:37.240
[CHOPPER]
To tell you the truth, I wish
I could stay here with you guys

344
00:20:37.240 --> 00:20:39.500
and study those plants for a while.

345
00:20:39.500 --> 00:20:44.140
I'm sure there's still a lot I could learn,
but the timing's kinda bad right now.

346
00:20:44.140 --> 00:20:45.780
Come back soon, okay?

347
00:20:45.780 --> 00:20:48.590
[NATIVE A]
That right! You
always welcome here, Raccoon!

348
00:20:48.590 --> 00:20:51.190
- [BIRDS squawking]
- [NATIVES cheering]

349
00:20:51.190 --> 00:20:53.760
Really? That makes me so happy!

350
00:20:55.090 --> 00:20:57.300
After my friends and I find each other,

351
00:20:57.300 --> 00:21:00.040
I'll tell them all about
this amazing place I found!

352
00:21:00.040 --> 00:21:05.000
And I promise, when I can,
I'll come back and visit, okay?

353
00:21:05.000 --> 00:21:08.000
Take. Journey long. Maybe get hungry.

354
00:21:08.000 --> 00:21:09.440
Oh, wow. Thanks!

355
00:21:09.440 --> 00:21:11.380
See Raccoon soon!

356
00:21:11.380 --> 00:21:13.580
[BABY BIRDIE chirps]

357
00:21:13.580 --> 00:21:16.320
Hey, I love cotton candy!

358
00:21:17.360 --> 00:21:18.830
[CHOPPER]
So long, everybody!

359
00:21:18.830 --> 00:21:20.790
Be nice to each other!

360
00:21:20.790 --> 00:21:23.600
[NATIVES]
Goodbye, Raccoon, you travel safe!

361
00:21:23.600 --> 00:21:25.060
Now that I've got a yummy lunch

362
00:21:25.060 --> 00:21:27.530
and all the cotton candy
I can eat, I'm ready to head

363
00:21:27.530 --> 00:21:30.070
for the meeting spot
so I can help Luffy!

364
00:21:30.070 --> 00:21:31.370
[gasps]

365
00:21:31.370 --> 00:21:33.570
[CHOPPER]
Wait, I just realized
I don't have a pirate ship!

366
00:21:36.800 --> 00:21:38.730
Why didn't I think of
this in the first place?

367
00:21:38.730 --> 00:21:42.470
I'll be there in no time flat!
You're so fast, Mr. Bird!

368
00:21:42.470 --> 00:21:43.500
[BIRD squawks]

369
00:22:11.740 --> 00:22:17.110
<b>Gloom Island</b>

370
00:22:11.870 --> 00:22:18.340
[NARRATOR]
This is Gloom Island, on the Grand Line,
home to the ruins of the Muggy Kingdom.

371
00:22:18.340 --> 00:22:21.580
An old castle remains from
the long-dead empire.

372
00:22:21.580 --> 00:22:26.320
Despite its age, a well-known
figure has made the castle his home.

373
00:22:26.320 --> 00:22:29.620
Why did Moria have
to get himself killed?

374
00:22:29.620 --> 00:22:34.630
[PERONA crying]

375
00:22:40.030 --> 00:22:41.470
[MIHAWK]
You're being a pest.

376
00:22:41.470 --> 00:22:43.570
Go and cry somewhere else.

377
00:22:43.570 --> 00:22:45.570
How can you be so heartless
when I'm grieving?

378
00:22:45.570 --> 00:22:47.840
Show some compassion, ya big meanie!

379
00:22:47.840 --> 00:22:50.000
Don't you have anything kind to say?

380
00:22:50.000 --> 00:22:51.430
Offer me a tissue!

381
00:22:51.430 --> 00:22:52.430
I'm your guest!

382
00:22:52.430 --> 00:22:54.570
Your manners are appalling!

383
00:22:54.570 --> 00:22:56.200
[MIHAWK]
I never invited you.

384
00:22:56.200 --> 00:23:00.040
The two of you showed up and
started living here without asking.

385
00:23:00.040 --> 00:23:04.170
Furthermore, this
article is not credible.

386
00:23:04.170 --> 00:23:05.230
What?

387
00:23:05.230 --> 00:23:07.870
But does that mean Moria
could still be alive?

388
00:23:07.870 --> 00:23:09.400
He made it out?

389
00:23:09.400 --> 00:23:12.340
A good question, now you ask.

390
00:23:12.340 --> 00:23:15.410
If he died, then I didn't see it.

391
00:23:15.410 --> 00:23:20.080
Although, if he did escape, then
I didn't see that either, I'm afraid.

392
00:23:20.080 --> 00:23:23.950
[PERONA]
But you think he might have survived and
they're lying about it for some reason?

393
00:23:39.910 --> 00:23:41.680
You can't fix that with your spit!

394
00:23:41.680 --> 00:23:44.020
Who even taught you that
garbage? Your grandma?

395
00:23:44.020 --> 00:23:47.020
[HUMANDRILLS yelling]

396
00:23:47.020 --> 00:23:48.520
[pants]

397
00:23:48.520 --> 00:23:52.790
Bastards, they may be stupid,
but, damn, they're strong.

398
00:23:52.790 --> 00:23:55.800
At this rate, I'm never
gonna make it to the sea.

399
00:23:55.800 --> 00:23:58.570
[yells, gasps]

400
00:23:58.570 --> 00:24:03.040
[HUMANDRILLS gasping]

401
00:24:05.040 --> 00:24:06.210
Hawk-Eye.

402
00:24:07.440 --> 00:24:09.860
[MIHAWK]
It's been quite a while
since you left the castle,

403
00:24:09.860 --> 00:24:12.800
yet you've only made it this far. Pity.

404
00:24:12.800 --> 00:24:17.440
And the boat I offered you.
It seems it's not seaworthy now.

405
00:24:17.440 --> 00:24:19.200
Shut up! It's fine.

406
00:24:19.200 --> 00:24:21.710
I can just hold onto
a few planks and swim there.

407
00:24:21.710 --> 00:24:24.310
I'm not one to give up
that easily, all right?

408
00:24:24.310 --> 00:24:29.410
Your sentiment is admirable,
but you can't defeat them.

409
00:24:29.410 --> 00:24:34.380
They're called Humandrills, baboons that
develop by imitating human behavior.

410
00:24:34.380 --> 00:24:36.380
[ZORO]
Humandrills?

411
00:24:36.380 --> 00:24:41.170
Had they grown up among peace-loving humans,
they would've turned out differently,

412
00:24:41.170 --> 00:24:43.070
but not on this island.

413
00:24:44.170 --> 00:24:48.150
[MIHAWK]
Up until seven years ago,
this was the site of a great war.

414
00:24:49.390 --> 00:24:54.990
[MIHAWK]
When I first came here to live, the entire
island still smelled of blood and smoke.

415
00:24:54.990 --> 00:24:58.600
Everywhere, dead bodies
littered the ground.

416
00:24:58.600 --> 00:25:01.090
As the battles raged on,
these baboons watched

417
00:25:01.090 --> 00:25:03.530
the violence between the humans unfold.

418
00:25:03.530 --> 00:25:06.290
In time, they learned how to
use human weapons and armor,

419
00:25:06.290 --> 00:25:09.270
becoming warriors of the forest.

420
00:25:09.270 --> 00:25:13.410
Humans can defeat ordinary animals
by using weapons and intellect.

421
00:25:13.410 --> 00:25:16.880
But what happens when
animals don weapons, as well?

422
00:25:16.880 --> 00:25:20.780
As you can see, they make formidable
opponents for an arrogant young man.

423
00:25:20.780 --> 00:25:22.190
You talkin' about me?

424
00:25:22.190 --> 00:25:24.070
Well, who else?

425
00:25:24.070 --> 00:25:26.740
Now, let's leave. It's late.

426
00:25:26.740 --> 00:25:30.590
The Humandrills won't
set foot near the castle.

427
00:25:30.590 --> 00:25:33.920
Yeah? You got no right
tellin' me what to do!

428
00:25:33.920 --> 00:25:37.160
I've got to make it to the sea!

429
00:25:37.160 --> 00:25:38.430
Of course.

430
00:25:39.430 --> 00:25:40.790
Do as you like.

431
00:25:40.790 --> 00:25:43.130
[panting]

432
00:25:43.130 --> 00:25:46.200
I don't care if they're
"forest warriors" or monkeys.

433
00:25:46.200 --> 00:25:49.340
I've already wasted enough
time stranded in this dump!

434
00:25:56.220 --> 00:26:01.660
[NARRATOR]
Meanwhile, on the floating island of Weatheria,
the world's foremost meteorologists

435
00:26:01.660 --> 00:26:05.480
are busy coping with
a most unruly guest.

436
00:26:05.870 --> 00:26:10.870
[HAREDAS, OLD MAN B panting]

437
00:26:16.650 --> 00:26:18.820
Get Haredas and he'll sort this out!

438
00:26:18.820 --> 00:26:19.980
Pretty please?

439
00:26:19.980 --> 00:26:21.850
[OLD MEN growling]

440
00:26:21.850 --> 00:26:23.690
We're old and you're scary!

441
00:26:23.690 --> 00:26:26.120
Who knows what kind
of trap you're plotting!

442
00:26:26.120 --> 00:26:27.720
This is a place of law!

443
00:26:27.720 --> 00:26:29.320
You'll be punished for your crimes!

444
00:26:29.320 --> 00:26:30.960
Yes, what if we shocked her?

445
00:26:30.960 --> 00:26:32.950
Or drowned her a bit?

446
00:26:32.950 --> 00:26:35.150
Which better befits a thief?

447
00:26:36.320 --> 00:26:38.320
Ugh. You guys got it all wrong.

448
00:26:38.320 --> 00:26:41.330
Please, let me out!
At least give me a trial!

449
00:26:41.330 --> 00:26:43.160
[OLD MEN]
No way, missy!

450
00:26:44.250 --> 00:26:45.950
[HAREDAS]
Hey, hey! Hey, hey, hey!

451
00:26:45.950 --> 00:26:48.080
Hey, hey! Hey, hey, hey, hey!

452
00:26:48.080 --> 00:26:49.590
Oh, hello, Haredas!

453
00:26:49.590 --> 00:26:51.540
[HAREDAS]
Hey, hey, hey! Hey, hey, hey!

454
00:26:51.540 --> 00:26:52.980
Hey, hey! Hey, hey, hey!

455
00:26:52.060 --> 00:26:54.120
Hey, hey!

456
00:26:56.610 --> 00:26:58.880
Well, well, what a pickle!

457
00:26:58.880 --> 00:27:00.150
Hey, young lady.

458
00:27:00.150 --> 00:27:01.250
[NAMI]
Hey, yourself.

459
00:27:01.250 --> 00:27:02.550
Another outburst!

460
00:27:02.550 --> 00:27:06.150
You just weren't made
to take it easy, were you?

461
00:27:06.150 --> 00:27:07.650
But never fear!

462
00:27:07.650 --> 00:27:09.360
You remember this fellow, right?

463
00:27:09.360 --> 00:27:11.060
Here, I'll show you a trick.

464
00:27:11.060 --> 00:27:13.690
Take your tightly tied
wind knots, like so...

465
00:27:13.690 --> 00:27:17.800
- [thud]
- [groans]

466
00:27:17.800 --> 00:27:20.100
[OLD MEN]
Haredas! No!

467
00:27:21.980 --> 00:27:23.280
[HAREDAS groaning]

468
00:27:23.280 --> 00:27:25.220
I was counting on you to help me!

469
00:27:25.220 --> 00:27:26.360
Get me outta here!

470
00:27:26.360 --> 00:27:27.490
I'm in a rush, all right?

471
00:27:27.490 --> 00:27:29.060
[OLD MEN]
Are you okay?

472
00:27:29.060 --> 00:27:32.260
Haredas, speak to us!
Tell us you're not dead!

473
00:27:32.260 --> 00:27:36.760
[groans]
Yes. Or no? I mean, maybe?

474
00:27:36.760 --> 00:27:39.670
[OLD MAN I]
She hit that kind and gentle man!

475
00:27:39.670 --> 00:27:40.700
What a beast!

476
00:27:40.700 --> 00:27:43.170
[OLD MAN J]
Doctor! Someone call the doctor!

477
00:27:43.170 --> 00:27:45.440
[NAMI growling]

478
00:27:47.300 --> 00:27:49.040
[HAREDAS]
That's most curious!

479
00:27:49.040 --> 00:27:52.510
So, she stole an armful of weather
balls and our research notes,

480
00:27:52.510 --> 00:27:54.080
then tried to make a break for it?

481
00:27:54.080 --> 00:27:56.550
See for yourself. It's all right here.

482
00:27:57.750 --> 00:27:59.830
Young lady!

483
00:27:59.830 --> 00:28:01.860
I'm a pirate. What did you expect?

484
00:28:01.860 --> 00:28:03.700
What's wrong with a little theft?

485
00:28:04.800 --> 00:28:06.660
Gotta make a living somehow, don't I?

486
00:28:06.660 --> 00:28:09.950
[OLD MEN]
Simply reprehensible!
Such an awful human being!

487
00:28:09.950 --> 00:28:14.130
We have a villain in our midst!
Whatever shall we do?

488
00:28:14.130 --> 00:28:17.210
Ugh. Just let me go.

489
00:28:17.210 --> 00:28:20.010
You guys don't want me here
and I don't want to be here!

490
00:28:20.010 --> 00:28:23.380
You got back everything I stole.
What does it even matter?

491
00:28:23.380 --> 00:28:27.200
Would you stop flipping out for five seconds
and listen to me? I'm in a hurry here!

492
00:28:27.200 --> 00:28:29.170
This is important!

493
00:28:29.170 --> 00:28:33.070
[OLD MAN I]
Don't get too close!
She's terribly violent!

494
00:28:36.170 --> 00:28:38.610
All right, I'm listening. Let's talk.

495
00:28:39.120 --> 00:28:43.760
Though I should tell you, stealing
a balloon was both foolish and dangerous.

496
00:28:43.760 --> 00:28:46.030
You need proper training to pilot one.

497
00:28:46.030 --> 00:28:47.990
You could've easily died.

498
00:28:49.980 --> 00:28:52.150
- [OLD MEN whimpering]
- [NAMI] Read the front page.

499
00:28:53.220 --> 00:28:54.920
[HAREDAS]
The paper, eh?

500
00:28:56.090 --> 00:28:58.990
You see that article about
the pirate named "Luffy"?

501
00:28:58.990 --> 00:29:00.730
He's the captain of our ship.

502
00:29:00.730 --> 00:29:01.760
Is he?

503
00:29:03.160 --> 00:29:05.300
Oh, I've seen that fellow before!

504
00:29:05.300 --> 00:29:06.870
The boy's a real upstart.

505
00:29:06.870 --> 00:29:09.540
Caused quite the ruckus
in Marineford, they say.

506
00:29:09.540 --> 00:29:11.760
He's famous for that
straw hat that he wears.

507
00:29:11.760 --> 00:29:14.200
[NAMI]
Our crew has been
separated for a while now,

508
00:29:14.200 --> 00:29:17.070
so he doesn't even know
if we're alive or dead.

509
00:29:17.070 --> 00:29:20.670
I had no idea what he was going
through until I read that paper.

510
00:29:23.140 --> 00:29:25.380
I've been taking it easy all this time

511
00:29:25.380 --> 00:29:27.940
while he was down there
fighting for his life.

512
00:29:32.350 --> 00:29:33.980
[HAREDAS]
Hmm?

513
00:29:33.980 --> 00:29:37.190
He saw his brother killed
right before his eyes.

514
00:29:37.190 --> 00:29:38.890
I didn't even know.

515
00:29:38.890 --> 00:29:41.160
I couldn't do anything.

516
00:29:42.460 --> 00:29:44.900
And now he's waiting for me.

517
00:29:44.900 --> 00:29:47.740
And for the rest of the crew, I'm sure.

518
00:29:47.740 --> 00:29:49.870
[OLD MEN gasping]

519
00:29:49.870 --> 00:29:52.910
Luffy is strong, but this
is too much to bear.

520
00:29:55.910 --> 00:30:00.250
I want to be there for him.
I want to help him.

521
00:30:00.250 --> 00:30:02.480
[NAMI crying]

522
00:30:02.480 --> 00:30:04.380
[OLD MEN screaming]

523
00:30:04.380 --> 00:30:08.020
Hey, hey! Don't cry. You'll be okay!

524
00:30:08.020 --> 00:30:09.590
[OLD MAN H]
Hurry up and let her out!

525
00:30:09.590 --> 00:30:12.020
[OLD MAN E]
We're the real villains! Look at us!

526
00:30:12.020 --> 00:30:15.030
Abducting an innocent young
girl and making her cry!

527
00:30:15.030 --> 00:30:16.300
[OLD MAN J]
Give Haredas the key!

528
00:30:16.300 --> 00:30:17.800
[OLD MAN K]
Quickly now!

529
00:30:19.500 --> 00:30:20.730
Let's sort this out and...

530
00:30:20.730 --> 00:30:25.100
- [OLD MEN gasp]
- [HAREDAS screams]

531
00:30:27.650 --> 00:30:29.210
[OLD MAN I]
That's odd. Where did she go?

532
00:30:29.210 --> 00:30:31.510
[OLD MAN E]
I don't see Haredas, either.

533
00:30:31.510 --> 00:30:32.910
[OLD MEN gasp]

534
00:30:37.480 --> 00:30:40.420
[OLD MEN]
Huh? How did she move so fast?

535
00:30:41.590 --> 00:30:43.420
Thanks for everything!

536
00:30:43.420 --> 00:30:44.390
Bye, bye!

537
00:30:44.390 --> 00:30:46.660
[OLD MEN]
Huh? "Bye, bye"?

538
00:30:46.660 --> 00:30:49.900
She pretended to cry
to take Haredas hostage?

539
00:30:49.900 --> 00:30:52.470
And she's stealing
our stuff again, too!

540
00:30:53.080 --> 00:30:56.880
[OLD MAN H]
The world below isn't ready
for the genius of our research!

541
00:30:56.880 --> 00:30:58.680
[OLD MAN E]
I know! I know!

542
00:30:58.680 --> 00:31:02.350
Take me to the sea! Anywhere!
I can't do it by myself!

543
00:31:02.350 --> 00:31:03.550
Impossible!

544
00:31:03.550 --> 00:31:05.290
[NAMI]
Make it possible!

545
00:31:06.290 --> 00:31:09.670
[NAMI]
Luffy, hang on,
just a little bit longer.

546
00:31:09.670 --> 00:31:13.860
I'm sorry. Every time we've been in
trouble, you've been there to help us.

547
00:31:13.860 --> 00:31:17.170
Just this once, I hope
we can return the favor.

548
00:31:17.170 --> 00:31:20.070
[OLD MEN]
Help! Thief! Get back here!

549
00:31:22.140 --> 00:31:24.340
You've already captured me, young lady.

550
00:31:24.340 --> 00:31:26.810
You don't need to pretend
to cry like that anymore.

551
00:31:26.810 --> 00:31:27.880
[NAMI gasps]

552
00:31:33.010 --> 00:31:35.850
[NARRATOR]
We now return to Future Land Baldimore,

553
00:31:35.850 --> 00:31:40.690
a mechanical island where the
genius, Dr. Vegapunk, was born.

554
00:31:43.510 --> 00:31:45.410
[MARINE C]
We have an intruder!

555
00:31:45.410 --> 00:31:48.040
[MARINE D]
Someone's broken
into Dr. Vegapunk's lab!

556
00:31:48.040 --> 00:31:49.210
What should we do?

557
00:31:49.210 --> 00:31:52.820
Dammit! Apprehend them,
but don't use any firearms!

558
00:31:52.820 --> 00:31:54.350
His inventions are too valuable.

559
00:31:54.350 --> 00:31:57.290
We can't afford to have
even one damaged. Understand?

560
00:31:57.290 --> 00:31:58.920
[MARINE D]
Yes, sir!

561
00:31:58.920 --> 00:32:00.190
[FRANKY panting]

562
00:32:00.190 --> 00:32:01.890
Get back here!

563
00:32:01.890 --> 00:32:05.090
Crap! They musta tightened security
after the last time I broke in!

564
00:32:08.340 --> 00:32:10.210
Hold on. I get it now.

565
00:32:11.310 --> 00:32:12.740
We can't shoot in here.

566
00:32:14.010 --> 00:32:17.450
[FRANKY]
Wait, what d'you mean
the lab is full of treasure?

567
00:32:17.450 --> 00:32:19.980
[KITTON'S GRANDFATHER]
Vegapunk is the head of the
Navy's science division,

568
00:32:19.980 --> 00:32:23.890
so all of his works are
valuable. Priceless, really.

569
00:32:23.890 --> 00:32:25.920
Our country's very proud of him.

570
00:32:25.920 --> 00:32:30.190
Although, I suppose it's his
mind that's the real treasure.

571
00:32:30.190 --> 00:32:35.000
At any rate, he spent his youth
working in that lab, tirelessly.

572
00:32:37.340 --> 00:32:39.040
[KITTON'S GRANDFATHER]
Have you noticed that mountain?

573
00:32:39.040 --> 00:32:41.180
A rather unnatural shape, isn't it?

574
00:32:41.180 --> 00:32:43.650
I never gave it much thought, but yeah.

575
00:32:43.650 --> 00:32:45.250
There's a story behind it?

576
00:32:45.250 --> 00:32:46.850
[KITTON'S GRANDFATHER]
It's a project Vegapunk

577
00:32:46.850 --> 00:32:52.190
began as a child. It was meant to protect
the island's people from frigid weather.

578
00:32:52.190 --> 00:32:57.260
He built it by transforming the animals
in the forest into a robotic work force.

579
00:32:57.260 --> 00:33:00.100
Unfortunately, it remains unfinished.

580
00:33:00.100 --> 00:33:03.720
It's a sort of geothermal system
to heat up the whole island.

581
00:33:03.720 --> 00:33:05.190
[grunts]

582
00:33:06.750 --> 00:33:09.920
The world just can't keep
up with his imagination.

583
00:33:09.920 --> 00:33:14.660
That's why so many of his works remain
buried here in a state of half-completion.

584
00:33:14.660 --> 00:33:18.990
Sometimes, the technology or
funds he needed didn't exist.

585
00:33:18.990 --> 00:33:23.170
Even though he couldn't get rid
of the cold, knowing that he cared,

586
00:33:23.170 --> 00:33:27.940
knowing that he worked so hard,
warmed our hearts at least.

587
00:33:29.650 --> 00:33:31.190
[whimpers]

588
00:33:31.190 --> 00:33:34.220
That story is super depressing!

589
00:33:34.220 --> 00:33:35.620
[KITTON'S GRANDFATHER]
Ya think so?

590
00:33:36.790 --> 00:33:41.060
[KITTON'S GRANDFATHER]
But the people here are happy to wait
for his return. Whenever that may be.

591
00:33:43.000 --> 00:33:45.730
Please respect our feelings
and stay out of that lab.

592
00:33:45.730 --> 00:33:49.910
After all, it's equipped with a self-destruct
button, in case you wanted to know.

593
00:33:49.910 --> 00:33:52.110
But why? Not the button.

594
00:33:52.110 --> 00:33:54.070
I mean, why did you think
I would want to know that?

595
00:33:54.070 --> 00:33:56.240
Like I was gonna press the dumb thing?

596
00:33:57.280 --> 00:33:59.510
Either way, that sounds pretty scary.

597
00:33:59.510 --> 00:34:02.130
Why don't we forget about
this whole mess and go home?

598
00:34:02.130 --> 00:34:04.470
I'll make you some nice, hot tea, okay?

599
00:34:04.470 --> 00:34:06.170
Sorry, kiddo, no way.

600
00:34:06.170 --> 00:34:09.700
I didn't come all the way out here
with no pants on just to turn around.

601
00:34:09.700 --> 00:34:12.840
I'm gettin' that icebreaker
if it's the last thing I do.

602
00:34:13.880 --> 00:34:18.440
Don't get me wrong, I appreciate your
hospitality, but I read the paper today

603
00:34:18.440 --> 00:34:22.480
and it turns out that my captain
has gone through hell and back.

604
00:34:22.480 --> 00:34:23.880
So, bye!

605
00:34:23.880 --> 00:34:26.080
You guys have a nice life!

606
00:34:26.080 --> 00:34:30.420
[KITTON'S GRANDFATHER]
I know it's tempting, but no matter what,
don't press that self-destruct button!

607
00:34:30.420 --> 00:34:32.320
Would you give it a rest already?

608
00:34:32.320 --> 00:34:35.360
Why the hell would I want
to do something like that?

609
00:34:35.360 --> 00:34:36.860
[KITTON'S GRANDFATHER grunts]

610
00:34:37.230 --> 00:34:40.530
I can't believe the doctor cooked up
all this stuff when he was so young.

611
00:34:40.530 --> 00:34:43.800
'Cause this is super brilliant
work if I've ever seen it.

612
00:34:43.800 --> 00:34:45.140
Half of this is so advanced,

613
00:34:45.140 --> 00:34:48.470
it'll take another hundred years
before the world is ready.

614
00:34:48.470 --> 00:34:50.210
Maybe I don't wanna mess with this.

615
00:34:50.210 --> 00:34:53.130
As a fellow engineer,
I gotta respect the man's work.

616
00:34:53.130 --> 00:34:54.400
Did you hear?

617
00:34:54.400 --> 00:34:56.500
The Marines came by and said
someone broke into the lab.

618
00:34:56.500 --> 00:34:59.010
That's not good. Let's just
hope they catch him.

619
00:34:59.010 --> 00:35:01.480
They're probably looking to
sell stuff on the black market.

620
00:35:01.480 --> 00:35:03.820
Even a blueprint from that
place would be worth a fortune.

621
00:35:03.820 --> 00:35:06.760
[MARINE A]
but so much as sneeze on one of
Dr. Vegapunk's masterpieces,

622
00:35:06.760 --> 00:35:08.680
and you'll spend the rest
of your life in prison!

623
00:35:08.680 --> 00:35:10.250
I don't care if you're a Marine!

624
00:35:13.500 --> 00:35:16.470
Sweet! He's got a pirate mark, too?

625
00:35:31.050 --> 00:35:32.450
[BOTH screaming]

626
00:35:32.450 --> 00:35:35.690
[CROWD screaming]

627
00:35:35.690 --> 00:35:36.760
[ALL gasping]

628
00:35:36.760 --> 00:35:42.460
[FRANKY]
So, hypothetically... if by some crazy
chance I press that button, like you said...

629
00:35:42.460 --> 00:35:43.370
[KITTON'S GRANDFATHER]
Hm?

630
00:35:43.370 --> 00:35:45.470
Yeah, go on.

631
00:35:45.470 --> 00:35:47.870
[FRANKY]
You wouldn't, like,
hold it against me, would you?

632
00:35:47.870 --> 00:35:49.810
[KITTON'S GRANDFATHER, KITTON]
– Of course, we would!
– Of course, we would!

633
00:35:50.810 --> 00:35:54.240
[NARRATOR]
News of this incident
quickly spread across the world

634
00:35:54.240 --> 00:35:59.100
and history would remember it
as "Baldimore's Nightmare."

635
00:36:02.730 --> 00:36:04.700
You're truly a blessing from hell!

636
00:36:04.700 --> 00:36:06.630
Thank you, Lord Satan.

637
00:36:06.630 --> 00:36:08.130
[laughs]

638
00:36:08.130 --> 00:36:09.170
[SATANIC PRIEST]
It's unreal.

639
00:36:09.170 --> 00:36:12.440
I never imagined that one day we'd
be able to fight back like that,

640
00:36:12.440 --> 00:36:14.810
much less beat them
and put them in a cage!

641
00:36:14.810 --> 00:36:17.480
The music...something
about it changed us.

642
00:36:17.480 --> 00:36:19.560
I've never felt so uplifted before!

643
00:36:19.560 --> 00:36:22.930
He's right! Courage and strength
welled up in our hearts.

644
00:36:22.930 --> 00:36:26.130
We stood up and defended ourselves
for the first time in our lives.

645
00:36:26.130 --> 00:36:27.260
[BROOK grunts]

646
00:36:27.260 --> 00:36:30.030
[SATANIC PRIEST]
Of course, we had no idea
how to use our weapons.

647
00:36:30.030 --> 00:36:33.170
Ultimately, you did most of
the actual fighting by yourself.

648
00:36:33.170 --> 00:36:34.470
But that's okay!

649
00:36:34.470 --> 00:36:37.310
What matters is the people who
were abducted came back safely!

650
00:36:38.310 --> 00:36:39.540
[BROOK laughs]

651
00:36:39.540 --> 00:36:43.690
No, you're too modest!
I only helped a teeny bit.

652
00:36:43.690 --> 00:36:47.630
Neither gods nor devils will help
those who won't fight on their own.

653
00:36:47.630 --> 00:36:51.200
In times like these, it is important
to stand resolute against evil,

654
00:36:51.200 --> 00:36:53.240
even if the odds seem insurmountable.

655
00:36:53.240 --> 00:36:55.770
You have the courage.
You proved that today.

656
00:36:55.770 --> 00:36:57.560
Such a wise god!

657
00:36:57.560 --> 00:36:59.060
You've inspired us.

658
00:36:59.060 --> 00:37:01.130
We'll do our best to make you proud!

659
00:37:01.130 --> 00:37:03.000
[SATAN WORSHIPPERS]
Thank you very much for your teachings.

660
00:37:03.000 --> 00:37:05.130
Hail Lord Satan!

661
00:37:05.130 --> 00:37:07.330
[BROOK]
I hope that repaid their kindness.

662
00:37:08.360 --> 00:37:11.360
[BROOK]
Still, I can't believe the news.

663
00:37:11.360 --> 00:37:15.230
Please stay strong, Luffy.
I hope you're all right.

664
00:37:15.230 --> 00:37:18.440
I'll be there soon
to share in your grief.

665
00:37:18.440 --> 00:37:21.140
If I had a heart, it would be heavy!

666
00:37:21.140 --> 00:37:24.010
Until I can return to your side,
all I can do is play a song,

667
00:37:24.010 --> 00:37:27.010
and hope that it reaches you, somehow.

668
00:37:27.010 --> 00:37:28.210
Damn it! Guh!

669
00:37:28.210 --> 00:37:30.600
I can't believe they got
the devil as their bodyguard!

670
00:37:30.600 --> 00:37:31.900
What an embarrassment!

671
00:37:31.900 --> 00:37:33.840
They should be the ones
in cages with those

672
00:37:33.840 --> 00:37:36.130
freakish single-jointed
arms of theirs on display!

673
00:37:36.130 --> 00:37:38.930
Actually, we could make a lot of
money doing that, couldn't we?

674
00:37:39.330 --> 00:37:41.070
[SATANIC PRIEST chuckles]
Good idea.

675
00:37:41.070 --> 00:37:41.940
[LONGARMS]
Huh?

676
00:37:41.940 --> 00:37:44.900
We'll put their freakish
double-jointed arms on display.

677
00:37:44.900 --> 00:37:48.410
They owe us and we can certainly
make a lot of money doing that!

678
00:37:48.410 --> 00:37:49.530
[BROOK]
Wait, just a minute!

679
00:37:49.530 --> 00:37:50.870
- [BROOK] That's wrong!
- [SATANIC PRIEST] Huh?

680
00:37:50.870 --> 00:37:54.020
And it's immoral! I'm certain
that you didn't appreciate it

681
00:37:54.020 --> 00:37:55.230
when they were cruel to you.

682
00:37:55.230 --> 00:37:56.790
[SATAN WORSHIPPERS]
Huh?

683
00:37:56.790 --> 00:37:58.960
[BROOK]
Everyone, listen to me!

684
00:38:00.130 --> 00:38:03.000
Let them go? How could we, Lord Satan?

685
00:38:03.000 --> 00:38:04.940
They'll just come back
and attack us again!

686
00:38:04.940 --> 00:38:09.940
No, they will not. I'll make sure of that
by binding them to a devil's contract.

687
00:38:09.940 --> 00:38:11.400
[LONGARMS gasping]

688
00:38:11.400 --> 00:38:13.870
[BROOK]
Heed my words well.

689
00:38:13.870 --> 00:38:17.240
If you break your oath with me
and commit a wrongful act

690
00:38:17.240 --> 00:38:22.460
against the people in this country
again, I will hunt each of you down.

691
00:38:22.460 --> 00:38:24.530
And then I will eat your heart!

692
00:38:24.530 --> 00:38:26.690
[LONGARMS scream]

693
00:38:26.690 --> 00:38:29.760
Thank you, sir!
We promise you we'll behave!

694
00:38:29.760 --> 00:38:31.830
We're going straight back to our homes!

695
00:38:31.830 --> 00:38:34.740
We'll never come back again,
oh, please don't hurt us!

696
00:38:34.740 --> 00:38:35.970
[LONGARMS grunt]

697
00:38:38.330 --> 00:38:39.630
[LONGARMS]
Now, grab him!

698
00:38:39.630 --> 00:38:41.440
[BROOK]
Ah! Woah!

699
00:38:41.440 --> 00:38:44.240
Wha... Huh... What's the big idea here?

700
00:38:44.240 --> 00:38:46.510
[LONGARMS]
Away we go!

701
00:38:46.510 --> 00:38:49.310
[LONGARM BOSS]
Sorry, but we don't believe in curses!

702
00:38:49.310 --> 00:38:52.680
[LONGARM TWINTAILS]
Also, your speech was stupid and you
fell for the oldest trick in the book!

703
00:38:53.130 --> 00:38:54.800
[LONGARM A chuckles]
If we bring back

704
00:38:54.800 --> 00:38:56.820
an actual walking, talking skeleton...

705
00:38:56.820 --> 00:38:58.360
[LONGARM TWINTAILS]
...we can make a whole ton of money!

706
00:38:58.360 --> 00:39:00.590
[BROOK]
Wait a minute! Let me go!

707
00:39:00.590 --> 00:39:02.560
I have somewhere I need to be!

708
00:39:02.560 --> 00:39:03.590
[SATANIC PRIEST]
Oh, no.

709
00:39:04.590 --> 00:39:08.820
We have an emergency! Lord Satan
has just been kidnapped!

710
00:39:08.820 --> 00:39:13.030
Everyone, prepare to summon
another devil and fast!

711
00:39:13.030 --> 00:39:17.170
Yes! We can still summon devils
with the magical power of underwear!

712
00:39:17.170 --> 00:39:19.940
[SATAN WORSHIPPERS cheer]

713
00:39:19.940 --> 00:39:23.610
[BROOK]
Luffy, when you
feel sad, just sing a song!

714
00:39:23.610 --> 00:39:25.880
Music is meant to make you happy!

715
00:39:25.880 --> 00:39:27.880
So sing as you wait for me!

716
00:39:27.880 --> 00:39:29.250
I'll try to...

717
00:39:29.250 --> 00:39:32.020
No, I will be there!

718
00:39:32.020 --> 00:39:34.830
Till then, if you can hear me,
